From 8e61afcf8888d55be88ba478af8aa61ff2adbcec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim <338195936+tim-meld@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:17:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] ggml: fused hyper-connection read GGML_OP_HC_MIX (CPU
 reference + Metal), qwen4exp opt-in via MELD_HC_MIX=1

One op replaces the ~12 small ops of a qwen4exp HC read (grouped RMSNorm, low-rank down,
silu, up, sigmoid gate, stream mean, inject projection) for batches of 1-8 tokens. Metal runs
it in three dispatches: inverse rms, down+inject (split-K, 4 rows per threadgroup, simdgroup
count capped by the pipeline limit), up+mix (simdgroup lanes split across the hc streams).
test-backend-ops HC_MIX 31/31 (f32/f16/bf16, nt 1-8). Full Q2_0 model: identical greedy
output; pp1 -2.7%, pp4 +0.6% (no gain yet; the HC read is bandwidth-bound on 1.25 GB of bf16).
